Title: 0005-amiga-quit-elif-key-q
Repository: grafx2
Base-Commit: f84cb09dc59d706d6e7b28778b01ba911f52298c
Requires: 0004-aros-stack-nostdiowin.patch
Author: aros-grafx2 project
Date: 2026-09-20
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: Amiga-family (AROS, AmigaOS, MorphOS). Not AROS-specific.

Problem:
  hotkeys.c used #eif and KEY_Q, so the Amiga-family secondary quit shortcut never compiled in. gcc 10 ignored the unknown directive; fixing only #eif exposes undeclared KEY_Q.
Solution:
  Use #elif and KEY_q (the only defined q keycode) for Right-Amiga+Q.
Validation:
  2026-09-20 AROS One x86_64 ABIv11 under QEMU: Right-Amiga+Q opened
  the Quit ? requester on instances C, A and D; Discard quit them. Evidence:
  docs/attachments/2026-09-20-lock-ilbm/instance-c-amigaq.png,
  instance-a-quit.png.
Removal:
  #elif/KEY_q is the real upstream spelling; keep it.

diff --git a/src/hotkeys.c b/src/hotkeys.c
index 9b5dc414..3b754859 100644
--- a/src/hotkeys.c
+++ b/src/hotkeys.c
@@ -1026,8 +1026,8 @@ T_Key_config ConfigKey[NB_SHORTCUTS] = {
     (KEY_JOYBUTTON+JOY_BUTTON_HOME)
   #elif defined (__WIZ__)
     (KEY_JOYBUTTON+JOY_BUTTON_MENU)
-  #eif defined(__amigaos4__) || defined(__AROS__) || defined(__MORPHOS__) || defined(__amigaos__)
-  KEY_Q|GFX2_MOD_META // Right-Amiga + Q
+  #elif defined(__amigaos4__) || defined(__AROS__) || defined(__MORPHOS__) || defined(__amigaos__)
+  KEY_q|GFX2_MOD_META // Right-Amiga + Q
   #else
   0
   #endif
